<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CBR011 Monitors Summary, ported from legacy's JasperServer report
  (cbr-legacy jasper-server .../CBR011_MonitorSummary.rpt_jrxml), its layout kept but for how it
  breaks pages:
  - Legacy had no groups: each detail band compared the row with the one before (by Structure #,
    then by inspection) and printed itself when they differed. A structure whose items ran onto the
    next page continued there with no structure header and no column headings, and a header could
    sit alone at the foot of a page. The structure block and the inspection line are group headers
    now: the structure's reprints on every page its items reach, and a group starts a new page
    rather than leave its header there without a line under it.
  - The title and summary bands, printed only for legacy's Excel export, are left out.

  As in the other reports, the port fills from rows rather than SQL - legacy called
  CBR_MONITOR_SUMMARY with a WHERE clause built as a string - every field already formatted as
  legacy's patterns printed it. The ministry line (the CBR_HEADER subreport) is P_MINISTRY, the
  logo comes from the classpath through P_LOGO, and Date Printed is P_DATE_PRINTED, in Pacific time.
-->
